 DevOps Interview Command Series — Jenkins (Day 4) ⚙️

Jenkins is one of the most widely used CI/CD automation tools in DevOps.
From building code to testing, packaging, and deploying — Jenkins pipelines drive automation.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Jenkins commands & essentials you must know:

java -jar jenkins.war

systemctl start jenkins
systemctl status jenkins
systemctl restart jenkins

jenkins --version

cat /var/lib/jenkins/config.xml
ls /var/lib/jenkins/jobs/
ls /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/

tail -f /var/log/jenkins/jenkins.log

curl http://localhost:8080
curl -u user:token http://jenkins_url/api/json

jenkins-cli.jar help
jenkins-cli.jar list-jobs
jenkins-cli.jar build job-name
jenkins-cli.jar get-job job-name
jenkins-cli.jar reload-configuration


🎯 Interview Focus
• Debug failed Jenkins builds
• Understand Jenkins home, jobs & workspace
• Automate jobs using CLI & API
• Secure Jenkins using tokens & RBAC
• Manage Jenkins as a Linux service
